# An answer of the wrong tag is a type error (Semantics rulings round 12, AQ): `Answer c`
# is the union of the answer constructors of row `c`'s tags, each typed by its tag's
# answer. Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
use Ui.*
use Fs.*

OfUi: fn Click, Contents -> [Answer Ui.*]
fn OfUi c, text = [[Ui.Button.Answer c, Fs.Contents.Answer (~ text)]]

Carried: fn Nat -> Answer Ui.*
fn Carried n = Ui.Button.Answer n

Unknown: fn Click -> Answer Ui.*
fn Unknown c = Ui.Knob.Answer c
